course: dictionary
lesson: 3698
title: Flatly: firm or dull?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing, and the sentence tells you which meaning it has. Flatly is one of these words. «For her cousin's wedding, Maddie flatly refused to wear a dress.» Refused is a clear no, so flatly must mean firmly, with no doubt at all.
explain: «The family steps out for the beach, the sky opens, and Dad says flatly "Oh, great."» The rain has spoiled the trip, and Dad's voice has no excitement in it. So flatly can also mean in a dull voice with no feeling. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Look for clues around flatly. Words like refused and denied point to a firm meaning. Words like sighs, bored or a soggy day point to a voice with no feeling. Watch for the phrases «flatly refused», «flatly denied» and «said flatly».
fact: Flatly is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Flatly» means completely and firmly, with no doubt: «She flatly refused.»
fact: «Flatly» can also mean in a dull, flat voice without feeling or expression.
fact: In a story, «The Rat flatly refuses» to leave his river, so he is firm and will not change his mind.
fact: Check the clues: a firm no means flatly refused, and a dull voice means said flatly.
exercise: «For her cousin's wedding, Maddie flatly refused to wear a dress.» What does flatly mean here? | *Firmly, with no doubt | Quietly, in a whisper | Slowly, one step at a time | Happily, with a big smile
exercise: Dad says flatly «Oh, great.» on the soggy beach. What does flatly tell you about his voice? | It is full of fear | *It has no excitement or feeling | It is loud and happy | It is high and squeaky
exercise: «The Rat flatly refuses: he's sticking to his river.» Find and copy one word that shows the Rat will not change his mind. | beach | river | *refuses | Mole
test: «Maddie flatly denied taking the cake.» What does flatly mean here? | Sadly, with tears in her eyes | Sleepily, after a long nap | *Firmly and completely, with no doubt | Very quickly, in a rush
test: Which phrase shows a dull voice with no feeling? | shouted with joy | flatly denied | *said flatly | flatly refused
exam: Dad says flatly «Oh, great.» on the wet beach. Which meaning fits best? | In a whisper so no one can hear | With great excitement and joy | From very far away | *In a dull voice with no feeling
